result:
The chart gallery now shows in view mode as well as edit mode. I haven't run tests, typecheck or typegen.

The cause was in `chartAlternativesLogic.ts`. The `isEditableSurface` selector required `editMode` to be true, and `canShowAlternatives` depends on it. In view mode `ChartAlternatives` therefore fell back to the plain `ChartFilter` dropdown.

I removed the `editMode` requirement from that selector and from its typegen signature. The other conditions are unchanged, so the gallery still needs all of these:
- the feature flag is on;
- it is a trends insight;
- the insight is not embedded, shared or on a dashboard;
- the user can edit the insight.

Everyone else still gets `ChartFilter`.

I left the `editMode` prop and selector in place because they are also part of the logic key. `editMode` is now unused in the selector, so removing it entirely is a follow-up if you want it.

In `ChartAlternatives.test.tsx`, the existing tests pass `editMode`, so none of them covers view mode. I didn't add a view-mode test. Say if you want one.
